    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-3">
      Linear Shower Drains: Single-Slope Mortar Bed &amp; Waterproofing Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      Traditional center shower drains require an inverted pyramidal or conical four-way compound slope. This forces tile setters to cut expensive large-format porcelain tiles into triangular "envelope" wedges so they can follow the compound curvature without lippage. A stainless linear drain revolutionizes shower geometry by enabling a <strong>single-plane mono-pitch slope</strong>, unlocking seamless large format tiles and flush zero-threshold curbless entries.
    </p>

    <!-- Key Metrics Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 mb-6">
